## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates practical CAPA thinking for data quality issues in streaming workloads, focusing on deduplication, regional containment, and fail-safes.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Evidence linkage
- Canary-based remediation
- Region-based metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Express API to create CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let capas = [];

app.post('/capas', (req, res) => {
  const capa = { id: capas.length + 1, ...req.body, status: 'Observed' };
  capas.push(capa);
  res.status(201).json(capa);
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for privacy-policy drift in a multi-tenant, partner‑integrated data plane. Requires data modeling, lifecycle management, API surfaces, observability, and rollout safety.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model including lineage and policy versions
- Region/tenant-aware metrics
- Lifecycle state machine and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback safeguards

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  rootCause?: string;
  correctiveAction?: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'investigating'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
